<title>USA: Nebraska cattle trade $1-$2 lower dressed - USDA.</title>
<headline>Nebraska cattle trade $1-$2 lower dressed - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>OMAHA 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slaughter steers and heifers traded $1.00 to $2.00 per cwt lower on a dressed basis, while prices were not tested on a live basis, but undertone decidedly lower.</p>
<p>Buyer inquiry fair. Seller interest unevenly good.</p>
<p>Live basis sales:</p>
<p>Slaughter Steers: No confirmed sales.</p>
<p>Slaughter Heifers: No confirmed sales.</p>
<p>Dressed Basis Delivered. Steers and heifers 1.00 to 2.00 lower.</p>
<p>Dressed Basis Steers: Select and Choice 2-3 1200-1300 lbs 108.00-110.00.</p>
<p>Dressed Basis Heifers: Select and Choice 2-3 1075-1200 lbs 108.00-110.00.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
